If you call logTableNames before creating tables, it will log an empty array.
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
await sdb.logTableNames();
await sdb.done();
```

You can use the stringify option to log all unique values as a JSON string:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Load your data into the table
await table.loadData("path/to/your/data.csv");
// Log unique values from the 'category' column as a JSON string
await table.logUniques("category", { stringify: true });
// Close everything
await sdb.done();
```

The getStdDev method returns a Promise that resolves to a number representing the standard deviation of the specified column:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
await table.loadData("./data.csv");
const stdDev = await table.getStdDev("height");
console.log(typeof stdDev); // "number"
await sdb.done();
```

Here's how to enable verbose logging for cache operations:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance with verbose cache logging enabled
const sdb = new SimpleDB({ cacheVerbose: true });
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// We cache the computations (verbose logs will show cache operations)
await table.cache(async () => {
  await table.loadData("items.csv");
  await table.summarize({
    values: "price",
    categories: "department",
    summaries: ["min", "max", "mean"],
  });
});
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

